5) Other
   -----
a. Mobile Pages will always create small parameter files in the directory
   m:\app\pages.  It will create this directory if it does not exist.

b. The file "pages.ini", contained on the diskette, stores information about
   databases held on the diskette, including their names and storage space 
   requirements.  It is used as a part of the PAGESmgr based installation 
   process described above and does not need to be copied to the Psion.

c. Contrary to general expectation, very often, searches on the database
   will get increasingly faster when you add more menu based search criteria,
   ie items that, having been selected, are displayed in the top row of
   the search criteria screen.  This position is only true when you have 
   the multiple types option set to ALL, ie all of the selected criteria 
   must be true.  The opposite happens when it is selected to ANY!

